    <string name="vmfix_patcher_section_signing">3. Signing</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_generated_title">Generated key</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_generated_body">Works everywhere. Termux must be uninstalled first, which deletes its data.</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_termux_title">Termux\'s key</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_termux_body">The key Termux signs its own GitHub builds with. The patched APK then goes over the installed Termux as an update and keeps its data - but only if that Termux came from GitHub.</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_termux_body_matches">The key Termux signs its own GitHub builds with. The installed Termux was signed with it, so the patched APK goes over it as an update and keeps its data.</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_own_title">My own keystore</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_signing_own_body">If it matches the installed Termux, the patch updates in place and keeps your data.</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_data_loss_title">This will delete Termux\'s data</string>
    <string name="vmfix_patcher_data_loss_body">The patched APK is signed with a different key, so Android will not install it over the existing Termux. Termux has to be uninstalled first, which removes the prefix, every installed package and the home directory. Sign with your own keystore to avoid this.</string>
